{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:1", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Mind is said to be of two kinds, pure and impure: impure when joined with desire, pure when free of desire.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:mind-cause-of-bondage-and-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:10", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "There is no dissolution, no origination, no one bound, no seeker, no aspirant for liberation and none liberated — this is the highest truth.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "notes": "Also Gauḍapāda's Māṇḍūkyakārikā 2.32 (variant reading).", "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:11-13", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "11-13"}, "paraphrase": "The one Self abides in waking, dream and deep sleep; the one being-self appears many in beings like the moon in water; as space in a pot is not destroyed when the pot breaks, the Self is not destroyed with the body.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:16-18", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "16-18"}, "paraphrase": "Two Brahmans are to be known, the word-Brahman and the supreme; one versed in the word-Brahman reaches the supreme. Having studied the books, the wise one devoted to knowledge should cast them away like husk after taking the grain.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:2", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Mind alone is the cause of human bondage and liberation: attached to objects it leads to bondage, free of objects to liberation.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "mana eva manuṣyāṇāṃ kāraṇaṃ bandhamokṣayoḥ | bandhāya viṣayāsaktaṃ muktyai nirviṣayaṃ smṛtam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:mind-cause-of-bondage-and-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:manas"], "cross_refs": ["tea:satyayani-upanisad:1-3"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:20-22", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "20-22"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge is hidden in every being like ghee in milk; it is to be churned with the mind as churning rod. The knower concludes: 'I am Vāsudeva', the partless, stainless Brahman in whom all beings dwell.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtabindu-upanisad:4-5", "source": "src:amrtabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4-5"}, "paraphrase": "When the mind, free of attachment and restrained in the heart, becomes non-existent (unmanībhāva), that is the supreme state; it should be restrained until it perishes in the heart — this is knowledge and meditation, the rest is extension of books.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:unmani"], "terms": ["trm:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
